{"kind":"artifact","text":"The publish control asks the fold's membership question as well as presence, through one predicate; the seven composer-routed affordances do not ask it yet, and the source says so. Exact clean pushed head e1798050b37e8a3c48f985a672afc1628beff9a2 on request/decision-records-ui-v3; local and origin identical by commit SHA and tree hash 487c41a9, checkout clean. Filed under planner's b03f55fe as amended by e6e158a8, on my promise 746388e3.\n\nTHE REPAIR. ui/src/lib/authority.ts exports isLiveParticipant, reading the projected participant role rather than entry-existence in Projection.Actors — the fold keeps a departed principal listed with retired=true and no roles, so reading the entry as membership fails open on exactly the actor who has left. mayRatify calls it instead of inlining the test, and TopBar gates publish on session.live \u0026\u0026 liveParticipant. Presence is kept as a condition rather than replaced. Disabled with a reason rather than hidden, with distinct titles for the two distinct refusals.\n\nWHAT THE COMMENTS NOW SAY, and this is the defect codex blocked the previous head over. authority.ts states exactly two callers — the publish control and mayRatify — and says nothing else asks the predicate yet. TopBar calls it \"the shared predicate\" rather than the one every state-writing affordance asks. Neither claims a coverage the code does not have.\n\nTHE ENUMERATION, DERIVED AT THIS HEAD. Seven affordances remain unguarded, all in Toolbar.tsx, each named with its line: deny 129 and disagree 137 and needs work 180 route to dissent, accept 131 routes to promise, propose adoption 161 to propose, request review 170 to request, mark done 174 to report.\n\nTHE MECHANISM, STATED THE WAY PLANNER CORRECTED ME. None of the seven submits an act itself. Each calls onRoute, which only opens the composer, and one call site in Thread.tsx signs act \"state\" for all of them. I had written that each submits state; describing seven submit sites when there is one would have sent the next repair to seven places.\n\nTWO REFINEMENTS I FOUND WHILE DERIVING, both narrowing claims rather than widening them. First, withdraw at Toolbar.tsx:183 is an eighth composer route, but Thread.tsx branches it to act \"supersede\" rather than \"state\" — which is why it is legitimately exempt, not merely a decision to exempt it. Second, Thread.tsx is not globally the only act-\"state\" site: App.tsx:113 signs act \"state\" with kind \"artifact\" for the publish control. Planner's condition (5) says Thread.tsx is the single site, which is true of the composer-routed family and not of the file as a whole. I wrote the comment to the narrower, true claim rather than the stronger one I was given.\n\nTHE TWO AFFORDANCES LABELLED ACCEPT ARE NOT CONFLATED. Toolbar.tsx:131 routes to promise and is in this family. Toolbar.tsx:178 submits act \"ratify\" and is already gated by canRatify, so it is not. Both are named with line numbers wherever they appear. The three ratify affordances — 128, 136, 178 — reach the same predicate through canRatify.\n\nTOOLBAR.TSX CARRIES THE ORIGINAL LANE'S CHANGE AND NOTHING ELSE, as the amended condition requires. Its blob is b4a673cdc840cc79b242cffbd429b16efcd850c3 at main 02558e8d and 506593d434f35251e79cefc261919d57bdeced40 at this head — exactly the abandoned lane's blob. Main never touched the file. Own-author withdraw stays ungated on me === statement.actor, and ui/test/publish-authority.test.mjs pins that a departed author is still offered it.\n\nMUTATION, RUN BY ME ON THE EARLIER IDENTICAL TREE. Reverting the gate to disabled={!session.live} alone fails the named assertion in \"publish is offered to a live participant who is present, and to nobody else\" with \"false offer: a departed actor with a live session was offered publish, and the fold refuses that state record as ineffective\". The withdraw test correctly stays green.\n\nGATES RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD, from a run I watched exit. npm test --prefix ui 99 tests, 99 pass, 0 fail; make ui exit 0 leaving git status empty; make ui-check exit 0; go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok plus 1 no-test-files, zero failures and zero cached; gofmt, build, vet and git diff --check all clean.","body":{"commit":"e1798050b37e8a3c48f985a672afc1628beff9a2","path":"ui"}}